<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Wheat trickles in from farms.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Wheat trickles in from farms.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers continued to sell small amounts of hard red winter wheat late Tuesday and early Wednesday in reaction to higher futures prices this week, High Plains grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Most basis bids were unchanged, but several dealers said pipelines were filled with wheat, which may soon curb buyer interest. Kansas dealers said flour mills there were well supplied with wheat.</p>
<p>Cash wheat sales increased this week as 30-day free harvest storage was about to expire, and more selling was expected as storage deadlines arrive this week or next week.</p>
<p>Rain this week, including more late Tuesday, aided the Kansas sorghum crop and farmers began selling small amounts of new-crop sorghum.  </p>
